// Up the flyer-tower (Bastion_3, the Guildmaster's window) and below it (the Vault). Pell's two plants:
// Voss's office and the chick's drawing (5.5), and the Vault's empty sixth slot (5.2). Pell opens the Vault from
// the office: the key is in the Guildmaster's drawer.

title: Office_Pell_Drawing
---
<<if has_flag("halden.office.pell_ledgers")>>
    Pell: The drawing's still there. He dusts it himself. The Wardens aren't allowed to. #still
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Pell: This is his office. Voss's. We're standing in the Guildmaster's office. Through a window.
Pell: There's a drawing on the wall. A chick drew it. A heron. Very tall. Holding a compass.
Pell: He's never surveyed anything. Not one place. I checked the ledgers, all of them, twice. #plant:5.5
-> Who drew it?
    Pell: It isn't signed. There's a name on the back. It's been scratched out, carefully.
    <<voice surveyor halden>>
-> We shouldn't be here.
    Pell: No. Which, technically, is why nobody's checked the drawer.
    <<voice warden halden>>
-> ...
    Pell: I know. It's a very sad drawing. I don't know why it's sad.
    <<voice drift halden>>
Pell: The Vault's under this floor. The key's in his drawer. Which, technically, is stealing.
<<flag halden.office.pell_ledgers 1>>
<<flag halden.vault_opened 1>>
===

title: Vault_Pell_Slot
---
<<if has_flag("halden.vault.pell_counted")>>
    Pell: Six. Still six. I keep hoping I miscounted. I never miscount. #still
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Pell: Seven slots. Brass. One for each keystone, the Guild says. For safekeeping.
Pell: Six. Which, technically, means seven minus one. Which means someone counted. #plant:5.2
Pell: And the dust in the empty one is younger than the dust in the others. A year. Less.
-> Isolde.
    Pell: I didn't say that. I'm not going to write it down. I'm not going to not write it down.
-> Who else has the key?
    Pell: Voss. Only Voss. So either he took it, or he let someone.
-> ...
    Pell: Yes. That's what I think too.
<<flag halden.vault.pell_counted 1>>
===
